A||||3||Formula88||Wiring Diagrams - Routing||||5||
Z||000000||Formula88||04-02-2001||11:56 PM||||Anyone have a source for a wiring diagram that shows the wire routing on an '88 Formula?  I need to trace a bad wire in my electrical system, but aren't sure where it goes.  I have the electrical diagrams in the Haynes manual, but they don't tell you how it's routed in the chassis.  Does the factory Helms manual have this info?<P>BTW, it's Battery Feed circuit 240 (orange wire) that feeds the 12+VDC Batt to the ECM.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-03-2001||01:21 AM||||That would be fuse link 'F' located at the junction block in the engine compartment to the rear of the battery. It is the only orange wire there, the other 3 should be red. The wire is incorporated in the engine harness and runs in front of the engine and then enters the passenger compartment above the computer box and toward the drivers side. It then enters the computer and feeds pin(s) B1 and C16, both of which are ct 240.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||04-03-2001||09:21 AM||||Great, thanks!  I figured it was a fairly straight shot to the battery, but since I thought I'd checked all the fuse links and they were ok, I wasn't sure.  Unless I've got a pinched or broken wire along the route.<P>Maybe then I can re-wire the car properly, so the ECM isn't running off of my cigarette lighter!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||04-03-2001||05:50 PM||||Shouldn't be too tough to install a new wire. Bad part would be to get the harness out into the engine compartment to do it!||||reg||1
